From c387ce5968307c2f624c8e0164a16dcf0982852b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiping Ma <shannonprover@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:44:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [chore] adapt to non-negative phoare bounds (EasyCrypt#1105)

EasyCrypt PR #1105 (`negative-phoare-false`) makes `conseq`, `bypr` and
`exfalso` on pHL judgements emit the side-condition `0%r <= bd`. Discharge
it at the 17 affected sites in SHA3OSecurity.ec, SecureRO.eca,
SecureORO.eca and smart_counter/Gcol.eca. In SecureRO/SecureORO the `fel`
step weight `i%r * mu1 ...` is replaced by `(max 0 i)%r * mu1 ...`, since
the former is negative outside the counter range; the sum is unchanged on
`0 <= i`.

Checked with EasyCrypt bb75dba5a (the #1105 head) merged on main 311ba5d17:
the `sponge` scenario passes except for the two SMT failures that already
fail on unpatched EasyCrypt main (SHA3Security.ec:835,
smart_counter/Gconcl_list.ec:192).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
